d economic control of the former Soviet Union to a more market-oriented financial system, reflecting broader global trends toward deregulation and financial independence. The central bank's formation was facilitated by key figures in Russian economic reform, including Anatoly Chubais and Boris Yeltsin, against a backdrop of tumultuous political changes following the dissolution of the Soviet Union in December 1991.

